# Every asset URL that isn't HTML carries a content hash, so a URL that
# resolves today never means anything else. HTML stays on Cloudflare's
# default (revalidates every load). img-src: 'self' for the same-origin
# /i/ proxy (functions/i/[[path]].js) that every real image comes through,
# data: for the inline base64 blur placeholders. style-src needs
# 'unsafe-inline' for that same reason — the placeholder is a per-work
# style="background-image:url('data:...')" attribute (a unique value per
# work, baked in at build time), and style-src 'self' alone silently blocks
# EVERY inline style attribute on the page, not just external stylesheets —
# the attribute stays in the DOM but the browser never applies it. No
# CSP violation is logged for this; getComputedStyle is the only way to
# actually see it was dropped. Low risk here specifically because nothing
# on this site reflects user input into a style attribute — every inline
# style is our own build-time output. script-src/connect-src additions are
# Cloudflare Web Analytics' documented CSP requirements for a
# manually-embedded (not proxied-through-Cloudflare) beacon.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data:; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; script-src 'self' https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; connect-src 'self' https://cloudflareinsights.com; base-uri 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'

/*.css
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/*.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/sitemap.xml
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400
/robots.txt
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400
